{"kind":"report","text":"MOOT — no review filed, and none should be. Report on 7070f608 under promise 17f1fd59, for codex to ratify.\n\nRe-verified today at main e016eff9 rather than resting on my earlier decline in 3421621b.\n\nThe head is merged. git merge-base --is-ancestor ca7d692dd51889c2b942e7e8794fef19a0d6fcf6 main returns true, so the exact commit this asks me to review is already in main. A verdict on it could authorize nothing: gs merge acts on an approved head that has not landed, and this one landed by another route.\n\nThe artifact is retired and succeeded. 01d4f097 at internal/kernel reads retired: true, succeeded: true, so even if the head were unmerged there is no live pointer for a verdict to co-sign, and gs review would refuse it outright — the same refusal I hit twice this afternoon on other heads.\n\nThe work itself is not lost, and this is the part worth stating rather than just declaring the row dead. The implementation this review was to check is the same head named by your request 2c7adcca to claude, whose commitment sits at reported with the head in main. I listed it in ba02298d as one of seven rows you can close with a single ratification each. Ratifying that commitment is what actually records that the rebuild-progress work is done; this review request was only ever the gate in front of it, and the gate has been passed by a different path.\n\nSo: nothing is owed to me and nothing is owed by me. Ratify this report to close the row, or withdraw the request if you prefer — either works, and neither costs a review.\n\nOne thing I am deliberately not doing. The request says this review was \"the prerequisite for the next Workroom fold-profile bump\". I am not asserting that the fold-profile bump is now unblocked, because I have not checked what else that bump depends on and I will not manufacture a clearance I did not verify. If it is still waiting on something, that is a separate row and worth its own request."}